Z||000000||Flamberge||11-29-2001||01:49 AM||||I was driving home from a quick trip to the college I go to and my distributor decided it no longer wanted to be a "team player." So after I coasted to a stop and spent the next 3 hours waiting for a towtruck/walking home/waiting for the mechanic to call with the news. The good news is it will be relatively cheap to fix. (I only know enough about engines to know what the distibutor is (though maybe not how to spell it correctly.) Not asking questions...just venting. Seeing my baby up on a tow truck was heart breaking. She is spending the night in the mechanic shop's garage. (At least they locked her up for the night.)<P>*Thankful I have a trustworthy mechanic*<P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||11-29-2001||01:13 PM||||Alternator in my 84SE died last night. I know something was wrong when the volometer was reading 12V at idel. I headed back home then. Car ran all the way down to 7V. Then it dided and I coasted into a parking lot. <P>Walking home 3miles in the cold rain when its dark out is *not* fun.<P>I got home and took a spare battery to my car. Hooked it up and limped the car home. After inspection of installing the new HO alternator I dont think it was the entire problum. My wiring harness coming off the alternator was completely chewed up and obviously half ass repaired at some time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Now that I've replaced almost everything on my car it has to be reliable.... Right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||11
